      {
        "id": "p4-p2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the average rate of change over $t\\in[1,1.1]$, $t\\in[1,1.01]$ and $t\\in[1,1.001]$. What value does the average rate of change appear to be approaching?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.1\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}$, $3.01\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}$ and $3.001\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}$, respectively. The rates approach $3\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}T(1)&=2\\\\T(1.1)&=2.31\\\\T(1.01)&=2.0301\\\\T(1.001)&=2.003001\\\\\\frac{T(1.1)-T(1)}{1.1-1}&=\\frac{2.31-2}{0.1}=3.1\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}\\\\\\frac{T(1.01)-T(1)}{1.01-1}&=\\frac{2.0301-2}{0.01}=3.01\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}\\\\\\frac{T(1.001)-T(1)}{1.001-1}&=\\frac{2.003001-2}{0.001}=3.001\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe average rate of change appears to approach $3\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-p2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p4-p2-b-definition",
