              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "instantaneous rate of change",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is the rate of change at an instant, or in other words at a specific value of ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "t",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " rather than across an interval of ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "t",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". Briefly explain the relationship between the average rate of change and the instantaneous rate of change.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The instantaneous rate of change is the limit of the average rate of change as the interval shrinks to the instant.",
          "worked": "As the second endpoint approaches the fixed first endpoint, the time interval shrinks towards zero. If the average rates approach a limit, that limit is the instantaneous rate of change at the fixed endpoint. Here the shrinking intervals beginning at $t=1$ give an instantaneous rate of $3\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C/min}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
